# Make sure bash and config files use LF so it doesn't break in Linux
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
# The reduced postal code dataset is regenerated byte for byte (plan 0060), so its line endings are fixed
libs/luna-shopper/postal-codes/src/data/*.json text eol=lf
# The DEZA fixtures are captured pages, stored exactly as the server sent them (plan 0085), mixed line endings included
libs/luna-shopper/deza/src/lib/__fixtures__/*.html -text
# The harvest document fixtures are regenerated by apps/luna-shopper-backend/harvester/tools/leaflet/to-harvest-document.mjs (plan 0086), which writes LF, so their line endings are fixed and a regeneration is a real diff rather than a whole file one
libs/luna-shopper/contracts/src/schemas/harvest-document/__fixtures__/*.json text eol=lf
apps/luna-shopper-backend/harvester/src/app/harvest/__fixtures__/*.harvest-document.json text eol=lf
